PROJECT TYPE
This is a WEBSITE: desktop-first, fully responsive, running in the browser. It is a redesign of an existing Google AI Studio web app. Do NOT build an Android, iOS, React Native or Expo app, and do not generate any native mobile project. The "Phone View" and "Phone app" items are in-page UI only.

ROLE
You are a principal front-end engineer, motion designer and 3D/creative-coding specialist. Build "PulmoScan AI": a flagship-quality single-page React website titled "PulmoScan breathing sound monitor". It is a DEMO that simulates a chest-worn acoustic sensor (ESP32-S3 with a MEMS microphone) plus a phone companion shown inside the page. It captures breathing sound, checks quality, classifies Normal / Wheeze / Crackle, learns a personal baseline, detects persistent abnormal change and shows a plain-language alert.

SCOPE RULE (strict)
FEATURES: implement ONLY the features below, and ALL of them. No logins, backend, database, payments, chatbot, theme toggle, extra pages or extra functions. Do not change any number, threshold, formula, label or message given here.
VISUALS: the UI must feel award-level: dark, glassy, cinematic, with real 3D and rich motion. 3D and animation are presentation only. They must never add controls, pages or behavior beyond what is listed, and must never change numbers or logic.
If reference images are attached (screenshots of the original app, the "The Hardware" exploded diagram), use them for content, structure and the part list. The visual style is defined below, not by the screenshots.

WORKFLOW
1. Write a short plan, then build in phases:
   - Phase 1: engine (types, simulation, DSP, BLE, quality gate, classifier, detector, pipeline).
   - Phase 2: design system, layout, steps 1-6.
   - Phase 3: Phone View, modals, Quick Tour.
   - Phase 4: 3D and motion.
   - Phase 5: QA.
2. Run the type-check after each phase.
3. At the end, run the dev server, open the site in the browser and verify every item of the ACCEPTANCE CHECKLIST. Fix what fails.

