QUALITY GATE (exact, quality-gate/qualityGate.ts)
For i in 0..min(dsp.windowMetrics.length, ble.windowTransportStats.length)-1: startSec = i·1.5 (2 dp), endSec = start + 3.
- Default: state VALID, reason "Good chest contact and steady Bluetooth link".
- Transport check first: lossPct > 2.0 OR maxGapMs > 20.0 → TRANSPORT_CENSORED. Reason "Lost while sending (<gap> ms gap, <loss>% lost)" if the gap > 20, otherwise "Lost while sending (<loss>% missing)".
- Otherwise, collect acquisition reasons; if any exist → ACQUISITION_CENSORED with reason "Bad recording: <reasons joined by ', '>":
  - clipPct > 0.5 → "sound clipped (X.X%)"
  - rms < 0.012 → "too quiet"
  - noiseFloorDb > -23 → "too much room noise"
  - contactScore < 0.58 → "loose chest contact (NN%)"
- Window scores:
  - wheezeRaw = max(0, (tonalWheezeRatio - 2.4)·0.24)
  - crackleRaw = max(0, (crackleBurstDensity - 2.8)·0.14)
  - normalRaw = 0.85; sum = all three
  - probabilities = raw/sum (3 dp)
  - acousticAnomalyScore = min(4.5, wheezeProb·3.1 + crackleProb·2.6 + max(0, 1 - normalProb)·1.4) (3 dp)
- Output per window: {index, startSec, endSec, qualityState, reason, lossPct (2 dp), maxGapMs (1 dp), clipPct (2 dp), noiseFloorDb (1 dp), contactScore (2 dp), rms (4 dp), wheezeProb, crackleProb, normalProb, acousticAnomalyScore}.

