- Controls: Link segmented [Bluetooth | Wi-Fi (dev)]; MTU select 185 | 244 | 512 (default 244); Packet loss slider 0-20% (mono value); Burst loss toggle; Disconnect event toggle; Auto-send to phone toggle (default on); Seed number (default 1).
- Transport stat cards: Sent / Received / Lost packets (e.g. 1628 / 1628 / 0), Loss %, Max gap ms, MTU.
- Packet strip: packets binned into about 200 cells (teal = received, slate hatched = lost) with 3 s window brackets underneath.
- Waveform overlay: rawSamples (faint) versus reassembledSamples (mint), with lost gaps shaded.
- Per-window transport bars (loss % and max gap) with the 2.0% and 20 ms thresholds drawn.
- Spec note: "Header 8 B + 236 audio B = 118 samples = 7.375 ms per packet · 16 kHz · 16-bit · 256 kbps raw."
- A "Transport loss never changes the alert score" card showing the current Alert score "X / 6.5". Beside it: a "Sync to phone" button (manual commit) and the baseline progress "X of 14 days" with an animated bar.
- Baseline rule: +1 for each synced session with >= 1 valid window, capped at 14.

BLE LINK SIMULATOR (exact, transport/bleLink.ts)
- audioBytes = max(20, mtu - 8); samplesPerPacket = floor(audioBytes/2) (118 at MTU 244); packet duration = samples/16000·1000 ms (7.375).
- totalPackets = max(1, ceil(len/samplesPerPacket)).
- RNG seed = seed·7919 + round(lossPct·100) + mtu.
- lossRate = clamp(lossPct/100, 0, 0.2).
- Burst mode: enter probability = lossRate·0.28; stay probability 0.72.
- Disconnect event: packets from floor(total·0.42) for max(4, round(140/packetMs)) packets are lost.
- Received samples are int16-quantized (round(x·32767)/32767); lost = zeros.
- Packet flags: 0x04 lost; 0x02 WIFI_DEV; 0x01 BLE. seq = i & 0xffff; version 1; byteLength = mtu; timestampMs = i·packetMs (3 dp).
- Track maxGapMs (consecutive lost packets × packetMs) and the per-window transport stats (loss %, max gap, lost packets, total packets over the packet range covering each window).
- Returns {packets, reassembledSamples, sentCount, receivedCount, lostCount, lossPct, maxGapMs, mtuBytes, windowTransportStats}.

==================== STEP 5: ABNORMALITY DETECTION (DetectorBenchmarkPanel, lazy, skeleton fallback) ====================
- Heading "5. Abnormality Detection" plus a coral-tinted mono badge "Demo data". Subtext: "Detects unusual and persistent changes in breathing patterns over 6 months of demo data. Alert level is scaled to 5.0."
- "Reset demo" button (restores Clear change, Run 1, #0001, Count bad clips on, 0.35).
- Controls:
  - "Scenario" select: Clear change (strong-prodrome) | Slow change (weak-prodrome) | Bad clips rise with illness (informative-censoring)
  - "Demo run (1–5)": Run 1..5 (= seed)
  - "Demo person": #0001, #0002, … (= subjectId)
  - "Quality Checking" toggle button labeled "Count bad clips" (informativeCensoring)
  - "Bad clip weight" slider 0-1 with a mono value "0.35" (the same tempering state as App; changing it re-runs the pipeline)
- Chart (canvas/SVG with animated line draw):
  - The y axis is auto-scaled to the Personal alert peak (e.g. 30.77) with ticks about every 8; x labels D2, D8, D15 … D180 (about every 7th day).
  - Header "Change starts: Day {changePointDay}" plus a legend: solid teal "Personal alert (peak)", dashed grey "Simple average (peak)", dotted "Fixed cutoff (peak)".
  - A dashed vertical coral line labeled "Change" and a dotted horizontal coral line labeled "Alert level 5.0".
  - Display scaling: each series × (5 / its own threshold), so every alert level reads exactly 5.0 (e.g. SR 40 → 30.77).
- Table "Live numbers from this chart (Demo data)": columns Method | Early alerts before change | First alert after change | How it works. The Personal alert row is highlighted.
  - Personal alert: "N days" (count of days < changePointDay with hbAlert) | "Day X" (first day >= changePointDay with hbAlert) | "Learns your own normal range first."
  - Simple average: same with zAlert | "Checks only basic day-to-day ups and downs."
  - Fixed cutoff: same with popAlert | "Uses one cutoff for everyone."
- simulateSubject180Days (exact):
  - RNG seed = seed·104729 + subjectId·7919 + scenario.length·997.
  - 180 days; changePointDay = 108 + (seed % 5)·4.
  - personalMean = 0.36 + (subjectId % 7)·0.055; personalScale = 0.17 + (subjectId % 3)·0.02.
  - Latent severity after the change (e = day - changePointDay, only for day >= changePointDay): strong = min(1, e/14); weak = min(0.54, (e/32)·0.54); informative = min(0.76, e/20).
  - Censoring: pTransport 0.06; pAcqBase = informative ? 0.08 : 0.04; pAcq = (informative AND toggle on) ? base + severity·0.24 : base. Draw one uniform u: u < pTransport → transport; else u < pTransport + pAcq → acquisition; else none.
  - Observation (uncensored only) = mean + severity·shift + studentT(6, 0, scale), with shift = 0.34 weak, 0.68 strong, 0.52 informative.
  - Thresholds: HB 6.5, z-score 2.45, population 2.25. prevSr starts at 0.3 and prevZ at 0.
  - Per-day record: {day, hbQcsr, zScore, population, hbAlert, zAlert, popAlert, censoredType, latentSeverity (3 dp)}.
  - Also build the 3-row BenchmarkRow table as in the source (detector names "Personal alert", "Simple average", "Fixed cutoff").
- Detector steps (exact):
  - studentTLogDensity(x, loc, scale, dof) = -0.5·(dof+1)·ln(1 + z²/dof) - ln(s), where s = max(1e-4, scale) and z = (x - loc)/s.
  - stepHbQcsr:
    - transport → return prevSr unchanged (surprise 0, evidence 0).
    - acquisition or null observation → rawEta = informative ? 0.52 : 0; tempered = λ·rawEta; next = clamp((0.65 + 0.85·prev)·exp(tempered - 0.14), 0.1, 40).
    - valid → altMean = mean + 1.65·scale; logH0 at (mean, scale); logH1 at (altMean, 1.12·scale); surprise = clamp(logH1 - logH0, -0.85, 2.6); next = clamp((1 + prev)·exp(0.62·surprise - 0.28), 0.08, 40).
  - zscore: transport or null → prev·0.85. Otherwise z = (obs - mean)/max(0.08, std); acquisition → z = max(z, 1.35); out = clamp(0.55·prev + 0.45·z, -2, 8).
  - population (mean 0.42, std 0.22): transport or null → 0; acquisition → obs + 0.45; score = clamp((obs - mean)/std, -1.5, 8).

