==================== AUDIO MATH (audioPresets.ts; deterministic; 16 kHz; 12 s) ====================
- RNG: Mulberry32 (state = (seed >>> 0) || 1; t = state += 0x6d2b79f5; t = imul(t ^ (t >>> 15), t | 1); t ^= t + imul(t ^ (t >>> 7), t | 61); return ((t ^ (t >>> 14)) >>> 0) / 4294967296). Box-Muller Gaussian with u1 = max(1e-12, next()). Student-t = z / sqrt(chi²_k / k), k = max(1, round(df)). range(min, max) = min + (max-min)·next().
- Preset RNG seed = 42 + presetId.length·131 + clampedBpm·17. BPM is clamped to 10-28 (default 15).
- Cycle = 60/bpm; inhale = 0.40·cycle; pause = 0.06·cycle; exhale starts at inhale + pause and lasts 0.46·cycle. Emit inhale/exhale spans (2 dp, clipped to 12 s).
- Base signal:
  - White Gaussian w: b0 = 0.96·b0 + 0.08·w; b1 = 0.88·b1 + 0.22·b0; b2 = 0.72·b2 + 0.35·b1.
  - Envelope: floor 0.03; inhale 0.24·sin(π·pos/inhale); exhale 0.19·sin(π·(pos - exhaleStart)/exhale).
  - sig = b2·env·1.15.
- Heart thump: heartPos = t % 0.88; if < 0.05 add 0.035·sin(2π·65·heartPos)·exp(-55·heartPos).
- Wheeze (exhale only): add 0.34·sin(π·exRatio)·(0.65·sin(2π·390·drift·t) + 0.35·sin(2π·780·drift·t) + 0.25·sin(2π·525·t)), with drift = 1 + 0.03·sin(2π·1.8·t).
- Crackle (inhale only): with probability 0.0028 per sample set decay = 0.65 + range(0, 0.3); while decay > 0.005 add 0.52·decay·sin(2π·1150·t) and then decay *= 0.91.
- Noisy: add Gaussian σ 0.26; for 2.2 < t < 5.6 add 0.85·sin(2π·145·t) + Gaussian σ 0.45; for 7.4 < t < 10.6 multiply the signal by 0.015.
- Clamp to [-1, 1].
- Titles: "Normal breathing (N/min)", "Wheeze sound (N/min)", "Crackle sound (N/min)", "Noisy / Bad contact (N/min)", "Your sound file", "Live Bluetooth sensor", "Live Wi-Fi stream".
- File decode: decodeAudioData; cap at 120 s; minimum 3 s; render mono at 16 kHz with an OfflineAudioContext; estimated alternating breath spans (2.0 s step, 1.65 s long); title = file name; breathsPerMin 15; always close the AudioContext.

==================== DSP (features/dsp.ts, run in a module Worker via useDspWorker) ====================
- Worker: lazily create new Worker(new URL('./dsp.worker.ts', import.meta.url), {type:'module'}); match replies by requestId; transfer a COPY of the Float32Array buffer; fall back to the synchronous runDspPipeline if Worker creation fails or onerror fires.
- STFT: N_FFT 512, hop 256, Hann window 0.5·(1 - cos(2πi/(N-1))), radix-2 FFT with precomputed bit-reversal and twiddles, 257 bins.
- Mel: 64 triangular bands from 50 Hz to 8 kHz, mel = 2595·log10(1 + hz/700); log10(energy + 1e-10) per band. Keep every Nth frame so the display has <= ~600 frames (stride = ceil(totalFrames/600) when > 600); melTimesSec = frame·256/16000 (3 dp).
- Per frame:
  - low/mid/high band means over bands 0-20 / 21-42 / 43-63
  - zero-crossing rate
  - spectral centroid
  - spectral flatness (geometric/arithmetic mean, capped at 1)
  - 85% rolloff (default 4000 Hz)
  - wheeze-band tonal ratio over bins 9..35 (max/avg, capped at 25, with a persistence count when > 6.5)
- Per 3 s window (hop 1.5 s; numWindows = max(1, floor((len - 48000)/24000) + 1)):
  - rms; clipPct = share of |x| >= 0.96 (as %).
  - noiseFloorDb = 20·log10(p10 of the 25 ms micro-frame RMS values).
  - Impulse rate = count(|Δx| > 5.8·σ) per second; kurtosis; dynamicRatio = p90/p10.
  - A mid-window FFT gives tonalWheezeRatio (bins 9-35, capped at 25) and bandSnrDb = 10·log10(inBand(100-2000 Hz) / (outBand(>2500 Hz)·0.65)).
  - contactScore = 0.92, minus:
    - clipPct > 0.3 → min(0.45, clipPct·0.15)
    - noiseFloorDb > -24 → min(0.45, (noiseFloorDb + 24)·0.04)
    - rms < 0.012 → 0.48
    - (diffEnergy/len > 0.12 and kurtosis > 12) → 0.28
    - (dynamicRatio < 1.35 and rms > 0.08) → 0.30
    - Clamp the result to 0.05-0.99.
  - windowMetrics entry: {rms, clipPct, noiseFloorDb, contactScore, tonalWheezeRatio, crackleBurstDensity (= impulse rate), bandSnrDb}.
- 21-D feature vector, exact label order: mel_low_mean, mel_mid_mean, mel_high_mean, mel_low_std, mel_mid_std, mel_high_std, spectral_centroid_hz, spectral_bandwidth_hz (= centroid·0.42), spectral_flatness, spectral_rolloff_85_hz, tonal_wheeze_ratio, wheeze_peak_persistence, crackle_kurtosis, crackle_impulse_rate, zcr_mean, zcr_std, rms_mean, rms_dynamic_range_db, band_snr_100_2000_db, inhale_exhale_ratio, contact_stability_score.
- Return {melSpectrogram, melTimesSec, featureVector21D, windowMetrics, dspTimeMs}.

==================== HB-QCSR SESSION SCORING (exact, evaluateSessionHbQcsr) ====================
- Constants: baselineMean 0.38, baselineScale 0.24, df 6, threshold 6.5. λ = the tempering value (default 0.35).
- Pool: VALID windows. If there are none and there are only transport-censored windows (no acquisition-censored ones), use the transport windows (the MAR rule, so Bluetooth loss never alters the score). Otherwise the pool is empty.
- acousticMean = mean(acousticAnomalyScore over the pool), or baselineMean if the pool is empty. predictiveSurprise = logH1 - logH0 at that mean (3 dp), or 0 if the pool is empty.
- acqFraction = acqWindows/windows; censoringEvidenceTerm = acqFraction > 0.25 ? λ·acqFraction·1.4 (3 dp) : 0.
- srStatistic = clamp(exp(max(-1.6, 0.72·surprise + evidence)), 0.18, 18), 2 dp.
- Status:
  - no valid windows AND (some acquisition or transport windows) → CENSORED_TODAY
  - sr >= 6.5 → ELEVATED
  - sr >= 6.5·0.48 → EARLY_WATCH
  - otherwise → STABLE
- contributingWindows (top 6 by contribution, descending): valid = max(0, (anomaly - 0.38)·0.85); acquisition-censored = λ·0.35; transport-censored = 0. Each has {index, startSec, endSec, qualityState, contribution, reason}.
- Do not retune any constant.

==================== PIPELINE & APP STATE (App.tsx; no persistence) ====================
- runSessionPipeline order:
  1. bleResult = liveBleResult ?? simulateBleLink(rawSamples, bleConfig)
  2. dsp = await runDspInWorker(rawSamples) (NOTE: DSP runs on the raw samples, not the reassembled ones)
  3. windows = evaluateQualityGate(dsp, bleResult)
  4. classifier = runRuleBasedClassifier(windows)
  5. trace = evaluateSessionHbQcsr(windows, validBaselineDays, λ)
- Result: durationSec = len/16000 (2 dp), sampleRate 16000, reassembledSamples from bleResult, isSynthetic = preset not in {custom, live-ble, live-wifi}, dataOrigin = the given value or derived (live-ble → live-bluetooth; live-wifi → live-wifi; custom → uploaded-file; else synthetic-demo).
- It re-runs when audioSource, activePreset, breathsPerMin, bleConfig, tempering or liveCaptureMeta change. A cancel flag discards stale results. isProcessingAudio drives the processing visuals (progress sweep, LED).
- Initial analysis placeholder: Normal 15/min; classifier 0.94 / 0.04 / 0.02 (7/7 valid); bleResult sent/received 1628, lost 0, MTU 244; trace baselineMean 0.38, scale 0.24, df 6, surprise -0.22, evidence 0, λ 0.35, SR 0.28, threshold 6.5, status STABLE; dspTimeMs 4.0; melSpectrogram [[-4 × 64]]; windows [].
- State:
  - activeStep 'input'; activePreset 'normal'; breathsPerMin 15; activeModal null
  - judgeModeOpen false; hidePhone false; standalonePhone false
  - phonePhase 'READY'; validBaselineDays 0; sessions []
  - participantContext 'Resting · Morning'
  - bleConfig {linkMode 'BLE', mtuBytes 244, packetLossPct 0, burstMode false, disconnectEvent false, autoSend true, seed 1}
  - tempering 0.35; audioSource = generatePresetAudio('normal', 42, 15)
  - liveCaptureMeta null; analysis; isProcessingAudio false; uploadError null
- Handlers:
  - Select preset: clear the error and live meta, set the preset, syncPending = syncImmediately && autoSend, regenerate audio at the current bpm.
  - Change bpm: set bpm. If the preset is not custom / live-ble / live-wifi, clear live meta, set syncPending false and regenerate audio.
  - Load wheeze sample: clear the error and live meta, preset wheeze, bpm 16, syncPending true, regenerate audio (wheeze, 42, 16).
  - Upload file: set processing, decode and resample, then clear live meta, preset 'custom', syncPending = autoSend, set the audio source. On failure set the exact error and stop processing.
  - Live capture complete: as described under Step 1.
  - Change BLE config: if autoSend is on and (disconnectEvent changed, or the loss rose from <= 2 to > 2, or from < 10 to >= 10) → syncPending true. Then set the config.
  - Manual sync: commit the current analysis to the phone.
  - Seed demo: generate30DayDeteriorationSessions(7) → set sessions and baseline days, phase RESULT. Clear demo: sessions [], baseline 0, phase READY.
- When a pipeline run finishes and syncPending is true, reset the flag and run commitSessionToPhone(result).
- commitSessionToPhone:
  1. Count valid / transport-censored / acquisition-censored windows; compute the dominant class (same rule as Step 6).
  2. Set phase ANALYZING.
  3. After 220 ms (clear any previous timer), append a SessionRecord:
     - id `sess-<Date.now()>-<day>`; dayIndex = count + 1; timestampIso = now
     - label = title; presetId; status = trace.status; srStatistic = trace.srStatistic
     - validWindows, transportCensoredWindows, acquisitionCensoredWindows, dominantClass
     - censoredReason only when status is CENSORED_TODAY: transport windows > 0 ? "Lost while sending (Bluetooth)" : "Bad recording"
     - isSynthetic
  4. If valid > 0, baseline = min(14, +1). Then set phase RESULT.
  Clear the timer on unmount.

